    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "Some of the Places of Interest\n1. The Monastery of Ling Yin\n2. The Gem Spring of Danc-\ning Fish\n3. The Cave of the Purple\nCloud\n* #1)\n4. The Dragon Well Dalley (/+//#)\n5. The Cave of the Morning\nMist and Sunset Glow\n6. The Tomb of Yao\n7. The Island of 3 Pools of\nMoon's Reflection\n8. The Chien Tang River\n(* * I)\n9. The Needle Pagoda\n10. The Tiger Run Monastery\n11. The Six Harmony Pagoda\n(JE\n(*\n12. The Cave of the Uellow\nDragon\n(# HE 70)\nLakevien Hotel\n(SE-LING FAN DIEN)\nHangchon\nROMANTIC HANGCHOW\nSOME FACTS ABOUT MANCHOW\n1. Once the Capital of China\n2.\n3•\n4.\nNow the Provincial Capital of Chekiang\n/½ million population\n118 miles from Shanghai\n4¼ hours' train iourney from Shanghai\n6.\n7.\n8.\n9.\nTo.\nII.\n530 miles of good motor roads\nWide, clean, well-lighted streets\nExcellent boating on the beautiful West Lake\nLovely walks in the magnifoent wooded hills\nWonderful shooting in the Winter\nAn ideal place for rest, recuperation or sport\nduring Spring and Autumn\n12. Lakeview Hotel has all the Comforts you desire.",
